WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.591
- [Narrator] Beginning as a friendly wager

00:00:01.591 --> 00:00:03.866
between Shell engineers in the 1930s

00:00:03.866 --> 00:00:06.855
about who could travel furthest
on the least amount of fuel,

00:00:06.855 --> 00:00:08.646
the Shell Eco-marathon has grown

00:00:08.646 --> 00:00:11.345
to become a hub of
technological innovation

00:00:11.345 --> 00:00:13.212
for generations of students

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:16.299
who are challenged, inspired
and supported by Shell

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:19.419
to dream up
ultra-energy-efficient vehicles.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.636
(whistle blows)

00:00:20.636 --> 00:00:22.686
- My name is Benjamin Esquirol.

00:00:22.686 --> 00:00:25.501
I am a part of the
Sask. Eco-marathon Team.

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.414
- Saskatoon, yeah!

00:00:27.414 --> 00:00:30.831
(upbeat inspiring music)

00:00:34.288 --> 00:00:36.307
- [Narrator] So, you've
been inspired to create

00:00:36.307 --> 00:00:39.150
an urban concept vehicle
for the Shell Eco-marathon?

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.991
Well, according to the team
at Saskatchewan Polytechnic,

00:00:41.991 --> 00:00:44.949
you will need the following ingredients:

00:00:44.949 --> 00:00:46.435
a lawn chair,

00:00:46.435 --> 00:00:48.043
a dismantled drill,

00:00:48.043 --> 00:00:48.876
a 3D printer

00:00:48.876 --> 00:00:52.619
(choir singing) and some inspiration.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:55.135
- Throughout my childhood,
I would play hockey games,

00:00:55.135 --> 00:00:57.385
and now that I'm older and in school,

00:00:57.385 --> 00:01:00.137
during my spare time,
I referee hockey games.

00:01:00.137 --> 00:01:02.227
(upbeat music)

00:01:02.227 --> 00:01:03.202
I joined the team.

00:01:03.202 --> 00:01:04.832
They put me on the frame crew.

00:01:04.832 --> 00:01:07.269
I didn't know what to
make the frame out of.

00:01:07.269 --> 00:01:08.904
Andrew explained to me, he's like,

00:01:08.904 --> 00:01:10.323
"I have an idea, crazy idea.

00:01:10.323 --> 00:01:11.156
"You wanna hear me out?"

00:01:11.156 --> 00:01:12.181
And I was like, "Sure."

00:01:12.181 --> 00:01:13.850
"What do you think of hockey sticks?"

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:15.783
- Carbon fiber hockey sticks.

00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:18.638
- Hockey to Canada is the
national sport we wish we had.

00:01:18.638 --> 00:01:21.055
("O Canada")

00:01:22.158 --> 00:01:23.625
Because Lacrosse is the national sport.

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:25.016
(music screeching)

00:01:25.016 --> 00:01:26.448
(light upbeat music)

00:01:26.448 --> 00:01:28.606
- With the Shell
Eco-marathon the goal is to

00:01:28.606 --> 00:01:32.310
reduce your energy consumption
as much as possible.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.660
We want to be responsible

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.469
with the resources we've been given.

00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:38.778
Repurposing the hockey
sticks, the water bottle,

00:01:38.778 --> 00:01:42.935
the body shell itself
is a recyclable plastic.

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:45.388
- We came in with no expectations.

00:01:45.388 --> 00:01:48.119
Actually my expectation was
to go around the track once,

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:49.872
and I would've been extremely happy.

00:01:49.872 --> 00:01:51.697
(car revving)

00:01:51.697 --> 00:01:53.937
(light upbeat music)

00:01:53.937 --> 00:01:56.950
The atmosphere at Shell
Eco-marathon is awesome.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.288
Everyone is interested in what you do.

00:01:59.288 --> 00:02:01.026
Everyone is very friendly and open.

00:02:01.026 --> 00:02:02.930
I would recommend anyone to come

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.136
who has an open mind and wants to learn.

00:02:05.136 --> 00:02:06.554
(light upbeat music)

00:02:06.554 --> 00:02:09.649
Every vehicle that competes
is completely different.

00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:11.258
(cheering in foreign language)

00:02:11.258 --> 00:02:12.551
(cheering in foreign language)

00:02:12.551 --> 00:02:14.589
(cheering in foreign language)

00:02:14.589 --> 00:02:16.513
Well this whole experience
is kind of life-changing.

00:02:16.513 --> 00:02:18.934
Until I was on the plane in London,

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:21.812
it just didn't seem real.

00:02:21.812 --> 00:02:24.483
They are looking for teams to come forward

00:02:24.483 --> 00:02:27.032
with new ideas and see what young kids

00:02:27.032 --> 00:02:29.074
have in their minds, right?

00:02:29.074 --> 00:02:30.854
We make the future, right?

00:02:30.854 --> 00:02:32.354
It's pretty cool.

00:02:33.314 --> 00:02:35.231
(ding)

